/-!
# The reduced ideal sheaf of an snc divisor: coherence and stalks

Hironaka's `red` of the support of a simple normal crossings divisor `F` is the ideal sheaf whose
stalks are the vanishing ideals of `|F|` (`vanishingStalk`); this module shows that these stalks
have local generators — so that `HypersurfaceFamily.idealSheaf` takes its first branch — and
computes them: at a point `a` with snc chart `φ` and indices `c`, the vanishing ideal of `|F|` at
every point `b` of the chart's source near `a` is generated by the single germ
`∏_{j : a ∈ E^j} z_{c j}` (Hironaka's
"the ideal of each irreducible component of `E` is generated by one of the `z_i`"
[Hir64, Definition 2, p. 141]; Bierstone–Milman's normal-crossings divisor, locally
`z_1 ⋯ z_k = 0`, [BM97, Theorem 1.10]). The proof is the classical one, made algebraic:

* near `a` the support is the union of the finitely many components through `a` (local finiteness
  and closedness of the components: `IsSnc.exists_nhds_support_eq`);
* a germ vanishing on the coordinate hyperplane `E^j = {z_k = 0}` near `b ∈ E^j` lies in the kernel
  of the restriction of germs to the submanifold `E^j`, which is `(z_k)`
  (`IsClosedSubmanifold.ker_restrictStalk_eq_span` with the one-index adapted chart); off `E^j`
  the coordinate `z_k` is a unit;
* the coordinates vanishing at `b` are prime elements of the regular local ring `𝒪_{M,b}`
  (`𝒪_b/(z_k)` is regular, `IsRegularLocalRing.quotient_span_singleton`, because
  `z_k ∈ 𝔪_b ∖ 𝔪_b²`: its linear part is the unit vector `e_k`), and no coordinate divides another
  (again by the linear parts), so a germ divisible by each of them is divisible by their product
  (`IsLocalRing.prod_dvd_of_prime_of_not_dvd`).

Consequences: the stalks of `F.idealSheaf` are the vanishing ideals (`stalkIdeal_idealSheaf`), its
cosupport is `|F|` (`cosupport_idealSheaf`), and in an snc chart the stalk at the chart's point is
`(∏_{j : a ∈ E^j} z_{c j})` (`stalkIdeal_idealSheaf_eq_span_prod`). These are the inputs of the
dictionary with Hironaka's predicates (`Hironaka/Manifold/Snc/Dictionary.lean`) and of the
monomial description of the boundary along a resolution.
-/

public section

open TopologicalSpace Filter Topology Opposite CategoryTheory IsLocalRing
